Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Omniphony (`bridge_api`, `liborender`)
   https://github.com/mgth/Omniphony
   Licence: GPL-3.0-or-later
   Used as a build-time dependency (pinned revision, fetched at build time; not
   vendored in this repository). viola-bridge implements the `bridge_api`
   plugin ABI, so the resulting shared library is a combined work under the
   GPL. The name and ABI of that crate are the interface this plugin targets;
   no upstream source is copied into this repository.

2. abi_stable — https://github.com/rodrimati1992/abi_stable_crates
   Licence: MIT OR Apache-2.0

3. Omniphony's reference bridge (GPL-3.0-only) was consulted as an example of
   how to use the ABI, and as the behavioural baseline this plugin is tested
   against. Its source is not copied: the WAV header scanner and the sample
   conversion in this repository are written independently, and the channel
   label table differs (16-channel 9.1.6 support is added here).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Steinberg ASIO SDK (used only by crates/viola_asio)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

crates/viola_asio implements a virtual ASIO device. It declares the ASIO driver
interface (the 21-method IASIO vtable and the plain-C ASIO types) from the
Steinberg ASIO SDK's headers; the SDK is not otherwise part of this work.

  SDK      : Steinberg ASIO SDK 2.3.3
  Fetched  : at build time inside CI, by scripts/fetch-asiosdk.ps1 (pinned URL
             and SHA1, verified on download)
  Status   : never committed to this repository (third_party/ is git-ignored) and
             never redistributed. No SDK file is staged into any artifact: the
             published artifact contains only viola_asio.dll + SHA256SUMS.txt.

Notice required by the SDK licensing agreement (section 3). This product
displays "ASIO" together with the following wording, here and in the product's
own documentation:

  "ASIO is a trademark and software of Steinberg Media Technologies GmbH"

The ASIO logo artwork lives inside the SDK (Steinberg ASIO Logo Artwork.zip) and
is not committed to this repository; the notice text above is displayed instead.

